      "source": [
        "# MiniMax H3 Ref2VA with SGLang Diffusion\n",
        "\n",
        "Run top to bottom in **Google Colab with a CUDA GPU**. This notebook starts one local SGLang server, submits an ordered set of image, video and audio references, waits for generation, and downloads the MP4 with synchronized audio. Keep the runtime connected until generation finishes.\n",
        "\n",
        "SGLang uses the official `MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3` root checkpoint and its `ref2va` partition. The earlier `abhishekchohan/minimax-h3-int8` Diffusers pipeline is **not** an interchangeable SGLang model path. Single GPU mode applies SGLang's supported `kitchen_int8` quantization to the official checkpoint at load time. Large GPUs keep the quantized transformer resident; smaller GPUs stream transformer weights from host RAM and may still be slow. Four GPU mode uses resident weights and parallel execution. First startup downloads about 108 GB of checkpoint weights and may need substantially more temporary disk and host RAM. You cannot assume a speedup on one GPU. This notebook has not been GPU tested in this workspace.\n",
        "\n",
        "SGLang H3 guide: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/docs/cookbook/diffusion/MiniMax/MiniMax-H3.mdx\n",
        "Installation: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/docs/docs/sglang-diffusion/installation.mdx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
